==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|targe}}, either:
* from {{der|en|fro|targe}}, from {{der|en|frk|*targā||buckler}};
or
* from {{inh|en|ang|targa}} (masculine) and {{m|ang|targe}} (feminine);
both ultimately from {{der|en|non|targa||round shield}} from {{der|en|gem-pro|*targǭ||edge}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*derǵʰ-||fenced lot}}. Akin to {{cog|goh|zarga||side wall, rim}} ({{cog|de|Zarge||border, frame}}). However, the soft -g- seems to indicate a French origin.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/tɑːd͡ʒ/|a=UK}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-targe.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/tɑɹd͡ʒ/|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑː(ɹ)dʒ|s=1}}

