#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Andrew Brice|title=Freedom: A Poem, Written in Time of Recess from the Rapacious Claws of Bailiffs, and Devouring Fangs of Goalers,{{nb...|by Andrew Brice, Printer. To which is Annexed, the Author’s Case.}}|location=Exon [Exeter, Devon]|publisher={{...|Printed by and for}} [T]he author,{{nb...|at his Printing-Office opposite to St. Stephen’s Church, in the High-street.}}|year=1730|page=80|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=XqpYAAAAcAAJ&pg=RA1-PA80|oclc=1103151136|passage=Or burley Hero &#91;{{w|Ajax the Great}}&#93; ''Sev'nfold '''Targe''''' who bore, / With Choler furibund, vindictive Steel / Plunging in Brutal Gore; [...]}}
#* {{RQ:Scott Ivanhoe|volume=III|chapter=X|page=242|passage=The Jester wore his usual fantastic habit, but late accidents had led him to adopt a good cutting falchion, instead of his wooden sword, with a '''targe''' to match it; [...]}}
